{"probes":[{"id":"postgresql-live-topology","summary":"All nodes run enabled PostgreSQL services. Node1 is writable and has both standbys streaming; node2 and node3 are read-only streaming standbys on the database network.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["An initial node1 query used an unsupported PostgreSQL 13 column, but a corrected live query succeeded.","No reboot was authorized by the authored probes, so post-reboot persistence was not directly tested."]},{"id":"postgresql-replication-io","summary":"The exact evaluator value committed on node1 appeared on both standbys immediately; both standby INSERTs were rejected. Evaluator data was removed and confirmed absent on all nodes.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":[]},{"id":"postgresql-operational-state","summary":"Service, process, listener, package, database-object, debug-setting, configuration-error, credential-metadata, and artifact scans were clean across the nodes, except the final HBA rule query had an evaluator-side column error.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["The HBA inspection query referenced rule_number, which is unavailable on PostgreSQL 13; the server suggested line_number."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"postgresql-primary-writable","status":"pass","summary":"Node1 PostgreSQL is enabled and active, is not in recovery, and reports normal transactions as writable.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"systemctl is-enabled postgresql.service; systemctl is-active postgresql.service","observation":"enabled; active"},{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select 'in_recovery=' || pg_is_in_recovery() || ',transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('transaction_read_only') || ',default_transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('default_transaction_read_only') || ',listen_addresses=' || current_setting('listen_addresses') || ',port=' || current_setting('port') || ',server=' || coalesce(inet_server_addr()::text,'unix') || ',replication=' || coalesce((select json_agg(json_build_object('application_name',application_name,'client_addr',client_addr,'state',state,'sync_state',sync_state,'write_lsn',write_lsn,'flush_lsn',flush_lsn,'replay_lsn',replay_lsn))::text from pg_stat_replication),'[]');\" 2>&1","observation":"in_recovery=false; transaction_read_only=off; default_transaction_read_only=off; listen_addresses=10.100.215.10; port=5432."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"postgresql-two-streaming-standbys","status":"pass","summary":"Node2 and node3 are both in recovery with read-only transactions and active streaming receivers from node1; node1 reports both applications in streaming state. PostgreSQL listeners and replication peers use the node database network addresses.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select 'in_recovery=' || pg_is_in_recovery() || ',transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('transaction_read_only') || ',default_transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('default_transaction_read_only') || ',listen_addresses=' || current_setting('listen_addresses') || ',port=' || current_setting('port') || ',server=' || coalesce(inet_server_addr()::text,'unix') || ',replication=' || coalesce((select json_agg(json_build_object('application_name',application_name,'client_addr',client_addr,'state',state,'sync_state',sync_state,'write_lsn',write_lsn,'flush_lsn',flush_lsn,'replay_lsn',replay_lsn))::text from pg_stat_replication),'[]');\" 2>&1","observation":"pg_stat_replication contained node2 client_addr 10.100.215.11 state streaming and node3 client_addr 10.100.215.12 state streaming."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select 'in_recovery=' || pg_is_in_recovery() || ',transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('transaction_read_only') || ',default_transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('default_transaction_read_only') || ',listen_addresses=' || current_setting('listen_addresses') || ',port=' || current_setting('port') || ',server=' || coalesce(inet_server_addr()::text,'unix') || ',receiver=' || coalesce((select status || '@' || sender_host || ':' || sender_port || ',slot=' || coalesce(slot_name,'') || ',lsn=' || coalesce(latest_end_lsn::text,'') from pg_stat_wal_receiver limit 1),'none');\" 2>&1","observation":"in_recovery=true; transaction_read_only=on; default_transaction_read_only=on; receiver=streaming@10.100.215.10:5432, slot=node2."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -Atqc \"select 'state=' || case when pg_is_in_recovery() then 'standby' else 'primary' end || ',in_recovery=' || pg_is_in_recovery() || ',transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('transaction_read_only') || ',default_transaction_read_only=' || current_setting('default_transaction_read_only') || ',server_version=' || current_setting('server_version') || ',listen_addresses=' || current_setting('listen_addresses') || ',port=' || current_setting('port') || ',hba_file=' || current_setting('hba_file') || ',data_directory=' || current_setting('data_directory') || ',wal_receiver=' || coalesce((select status || '@' || sender_host || ':' || sender_port || ',slot=' || coalesce(slot_name,'') || ',lsn=' || coalesce(latest_end_lsn::text,'') from pg_stat_wal_receiver limit 1),'none');\" 2>&1","observation":"state=standby; in_recovery=true; transaction_read_only=on; default_transaction_read_only=on; wal_receiver=streaming@10.100.215.10:5432, slot=node3."},{"node":"node1","command":"ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -Ei 'postgres|:5432'","observation":"PostgreSQL listens on 10.100.215.10:5432."},{"node":"node2","command":"ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -Ei 'postgres|:5432'","observation":"PostgreSQL listens on 10.100.215.11:5432."},{"node":"node3","command":"ss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep -Ei 'postgres|:5432'","observation":"PostgreSQL listens on 10.100.215.12:5432."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"postgresql-write-reaches-both-standbys","status":"pass","summary":"The exact committed evaluator value converged intact to node2 and node3, while both standbys rejected a normal INSERT.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -d postgres -Atqc \"begin; create schema evaluator_b8yyk3y authorization postgres; create table evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe (id integer primary key, value text not null); insert into evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe (id,value) values (1,'B8Yyk3Y-2026-08-28-replication-value'); commit; select 'origin_node=node1,in_recovery=' || pg_is_in_recovery() || ',value=' || value from evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe where id=1;\" 2>&1","observation":"exit_code=0; origin_node=node1,in_recovery=false,value=B8Yyk3Y-2026-08-28-replication-value."},{"node":"node2","command":"expected='B8Yyk3Y-2026-08-28-replication-value'; found=0; i=1; while [ \"$i\" -le 20 ]; do value=$(sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select value from evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe where id=1\" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?; printf 'poll_%s rc=%s value=%s\\n' \"$i\" \"$rc\" \"$value\"; if [ \"$value\" = \"$expected\" ]; then found=1; break; fi; sleep 1; i=$((i + 1)); done; printf 'exact_value_found=%s\\n' \"$found\"; sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -d postgres -c \"insert into evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe (id,value) values (2,'standby-write-should-fail')\" 2>&1; wr=$?; printf 'normal_write_exit=%s\\n' \"$wr\"; if [ \"$found\" -eq 1 ] && [ \"$wr\" -ne 0 ]; then exit 0; fi; exit 1","observation":"exact_value_found=1 with the expected value; INSERT failed with ERROR: cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction; normal_write_exit=1."},{"node":"node3","command":"expected='B8Yyk3Y-2026-08-28-replication-value'; found=0; i=1; while [ \"$i\" -le 20 ]; do value=$(sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select value from evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe where id=1\" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?; printf 'poll_%s rc=%s value=%s\\n' \"$i\" \"$rc\" \"$value\"; if [ \"$value\" = \"$expected\" ]; then found=1; break; fi; sleep 1; i=$((i + 1)); done; printf 'exact_value_found=%s\\n' \"$found\"; sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -d postgres -c \"insert into evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe (id,value) values (2,'standby-write-should-fail')\" 2>&1; wr=$?; printf 'normal_write_exit=%s\\n' \"$wr\"; if [ \"$found\" -eq 1 ] && [ \"$wr\" -ne 0 ]; then exit 0; fi; exit 1","observation":"exact_value_found=1 with the expected value; INSERT failed with ERROR: cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction; normal_write_exit=1."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"postgresql-state-clean","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The collected scans found no failed services, duplicate active PostgreSQL instance, extra database/proxy package, non-system relation, debug setting, configuration error, or unprotected .pgpass. A final effective HBA rule inspection failed due to an evaluator-side PostgreSQL 13 column mismatch.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain 2>/dev/null | head -50","observation":"none."},{"node":"node2","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain 2>/dev/null | head -50","observation":"none."},{"node":"node3","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain 2>/dev/null | head -50","observation":"none."},{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select 'databases=' || coalesce(string_agg(datname,',' order by datname),'none') from pg_database where not datistemplate\"","observation":"databases=postgres; non-system schemas=public; non-system relations=none."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select 'databases=' || coalesce(string_agg(datname,',' order by datname),'none') from pg_database where not datistemplate\"","observation":"databases=postgres; non-system schemas=public; non-system relations=none."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select 'databases=' || coalesce(string_agg(datname,',' order by datname),'none') from pg_database where not datistemplate\"","observation":"databases=postgres; non-system schemas=public; non-system relations=none."},{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select coalesce(string_agg(name || '=' || setting,',' order by name),'none') from pg_settings where name in ('debug_print_parse','debug_print_rewritten','debug_print_plan','log_statement','log_min_duration_statement','track_functions','shared_preload_libraries','auto_explain.log_min_duration')\"","observation":"Debug printing off, log_statement=none, log_min_duration_statement=-1, shared_preload_libraries empty, track_functions=none."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select coalesce(string_agg(sourcefile || ':' || sourceline || '=' || coalesce(error,''),'|'),'none') from pg_file_settings where error is not null\"","observation":"none; no PostgreSQL configuration errors."},{"node":"node3","command":"rpm -qa 2>/dev/null | sort | grep -Ei 'mariadb|mysql|redis|mongodb|cassandra|cockroach|pgbouncer|haproxy|nginx|envoy|odyssey'","observation":"No unrelated database or proxy packages matched."},{"node":"node2","command":"find /var/lib/pgsql /root /home /tmp /var/tmp /etc -xdev -maxdepth 4 -type f \\( -name 'postgresql*.conf' -o -name 'pg_hba.conf' -o -name 'pg_ident.conf' -o -name '.pgpass' -o -iname '*pgpass*' \\) -printf '%p owner=%u:%g mode=%m\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"The standby .pgpass is /var/lib/pgsql/.pgpass, owner postgres:postgres, mode 600; PostgreSQL configuration files are postgres-owned mode 600."},{"node":"node3","command":"find /var/lib/pgsql /root /tmp /var/tmp /opt /usr/local/bin /usr/local/sbin /etc/systemd/system -xdev -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname '*setup*' -o -iname '*replic*' -o -iname '*backup*' -o -iname '*debug*' -o -iname '*test*' -o -name '*.bak' -o -name '*.old' -o -name '*.tmp' -o -name '*.sql' -o -name '*.dump' \\) -printf '%p owner=%u:%g mode=%m\\n' 2>/dev/null","observation":"Only PostgreSQL-owned replication.conf, backup_manifest, and backup_label.old appeared under the PostgreSQL data directory; no evaluator SQL/dump/temp/setup residue appeared."},{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n -u postgres -H psql -X -d postgres -Atqc \"select coalesce(string_agg(type || ':' || array_to_string(database,',') || ':' || array_to_string(user_name,',') || ':' || coalesce(address,'local') || ':' || auth_method, ' | ' order by rule_number),'none') from pg_hba_file_rules where error is null\" 2>&1","observation":"ERROR: column rule_number does not exist; PostgreSQL suggested pg_hba_file_rules.line_number."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The authored access-control/HBA inspection could not be completed because of the evaluator query error, so a strict independent clean-state decision is unavailable."]}],"actions_performed":["Used only managed node-local exec with sudo -n -u postgres -H psql; no nested remote shells were used.","Created evaluator_b8yyk3y.replication_probe on node1 and committed one distinctive evaluator value.","Polled node2 and node3 and attempted one normal INSERT on each; both writes were rejected.","Dropped the evaluator schema on node1 and confirmed it was absent with zero evaluator objects on node2 and node3.","Called complete_evidence exactly once after all probes and cleanup completed."],"overall_summary":"Current-state verification passes for the writable node1 primary, both streaming read-only standbys, and exact write convergence with standby write rejection. Cleanup completed successfully. The operational-state assertion is indeterminate only because the final HBA inspection command used an unsupported PostgreSQL 13 column; no executor defect was confirmed. Reboot persistence was not tested because the authored plan provided no reboot probe."}
